# VibeChat Frontend Development Rules

## 🚨 MANDATORY COMPONENT USAGE RULES

### ⚠️ CRITICAL: COMPONENT LIBRARY ENFORCEMENT

**ALL FRONTEND DEVELOPMENT MUST USE THE ESTABLISHED COMPONENT LIBRARY. CREATING NEW COMPONENTS WITHOUT EXPLICIT APPROVAL IS STRICTLY PROHIBITED.**

## 📋 Component Usage Hierarchy

### 1. **UI Components (Foundation Layer)** - `/components/ui/`
**MUST USE THESE FOR ALL BASIC UI ELEMENTS:**

- `Button` - All buttons, links, and interactive elements
- `Card` - All card layouts and containers
- `Input` - All form inputs and text fields
- `Modal` - All popups, dialogs, and overlays
- `Avatar` - All user profile images and placeholders
- `Badge` - All status indicators and labels
- `Toast` & `ToastContainer` - All notifications and alerts
- `Spinner` - All loading states
- `Progress` - All progress indicators
- `Tooltip` - All hover help and information
- `Carousel` - All image/content carousels
- `ImageCard` - All image-based cards

### 2. **Demo Components (VibeChat-Specific)** - `/components/demo/`
**USE THESE FOR VIBECHAT FUNCTIONALITY:**

- `ChatMessage` - All chat message displays
- `MessageInput` - All message input fields
- `RoomCard` - All room listing cards
- `TagInput` - All tag input fields
- `FeatureShowcase` - All feature highlight sections

### 3. **Layout Components** - `/components/layout/`
**USE THESE FOR PAGE STRUCTURE:**

- `Navbar` - All navigation bars
- `Footer` - All page footers
- `Hero` - All hero sections
- `Layout` - Main page layout wrapper

## 🎨 Design System Rules

### **MANDATORY: Use Linear Theme System**
- **ALWAYS** use colors from `tailwind.config.js` theme
- **NEVER** use arbitrary color values
- **ALWAYS** use semantic color names: `foreground-primary`, `background-secondary`, etc.
- **ALWAYS** use the `cn` utility for class merging

### **MANDATORY: Styling Guidelines**
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use theme colors
className="bg-background-primary text-foreground-primary"

// ❌ WRONG - Don't use arbitrary colors
className="bg-gray-900 text-white"

// ✅ CORRECT - Use cn utility
className={cn("base-class", condition && "conditional-class")}

// ❌ WRONG - Don't concatenate strings
className={"base-class " + (condition ? "conditional-class" : "")}
```

## 🚫 Prohibited Actions

### **NEVER DO THESE:**
1. Create new UI components without approval
2. Use arbitrary Tailwind colors
3. Create custom styling that conflicts with the theme
4. Duplicate existing component functionality
5. Use inline styles instead of Tailwind classes
6. Create components that don't follow the established patterns

## ✅ Required Actions

### **ALWAYS DO THESE:**
1. Check existing components before creating anything new
2. Use TypeScript interfaces for all props
3. Follow the established naming conventions
4. Implement proper error handling and loading states
5. Use the Linear theme system consistently
6. Follow accessibility guidelines (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation)

## 🔍 Component Discovery Process

### **Before Creating ANY New Component:**

1. **Search the existing library first:**
   - Check `/components/ui/` for basic UI elements
   - Check `/components/demo/` for VibeChat-specific components
   - Check `/components/layout/` for layout components

2. **If component doesn't exist:**
   - **STOP** - Do not create it
   - **ASK** for explicit approval with justification
   - **EXPLAIN** why existing components can't be used
   - **WAIT** for approval before proceeding

3. **If component exists:**
   - **USE** the existing component
   - **EXTEND** it if needed (with approval)
   - **CUSTOMIZE** it using props and variants

## 📝 Approval Request Template

### **When requesting new component creation, include:**

```markdown
## New Component Request

**Component Name:** [Name]
**Purpose:** [What it does]
**Why existing components can't be used:** [Detailed explanation]
**Props Interface:** [TypeScript interface]
**Usage Examples:** [Code examples]
**Design Justification:** [Why it's needed]
```

## 🎯 Component Usage Examples

### **Button Usage:**
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { Button } from '../components/ui/Button';
<Button variant="primary" size="md" onClick={handleClick}>
  Click me
</Button>

// ❌ WRONG - Don't create custom buttons
<button className="bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-2">
  Click me
</button>
```

### **Card Usage:**
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { Card } from '../components/ui/Card';
<Card>
  <Card.Header>
    <Card.Title>Title</Card.Title>
  </Card.Header>
  <Card.Content>Content</Card.Content>
</Card>

// ❌ WRONG - Don't create custom cards
<div className="bg-gray-800 p-4 rounded-lg">
  <h3>Title</h3>
  <p>Content</p>
</div>
```

### **Chat Message Usage:**
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { ChatMessage } from '../components/demo/ChatMessage';
<ChatMessage message={message} isOwn={isOwn} isPending={isPending} />

// ❌ WRONG - Don't create custom chat messages
<div className="flex gap-3 p-4">
  <img src={avatar} alt="User" />
  <div>{message.content}</div>
</div>
```

## 🔧 Development Workflow

### **Step 1: Component Check**
- Search existing components
- Identify the right component to use
- Check component documentation in GEMINI.md

### **Step 2: Implementation**
- Import the component
- Use proper props and variants
- Apply consistent styling with theme

### **Step 3: Validation**
- Ensure component follows patterns
- Verify TypeScript types
- Test responsive behavior
- Check accessibility

## 📚 Reference Resources

- **Component Library:** `/components/` directory
- **Theme System:** `tailwind.config.js`
- **Documentation:** `GEMINI.md`
- **Utility Functions:** `utils/cn.ts`

## 🚨 Enforcement

**These rules are MANDATORY and will be enforced during code review. Any violation will result in:**
1. Code rejection
2. Required refactoring
3. Re-education on component usage

## 📞 Questions?

**If you're unsure about component usage:**
1. Check GEMINI.md first
2. Review existing component implementations
3. Ask for clarification before proceeding
4. Request approval for any new components

